/* ---- HL 1.1.0.0 - 1.1.0.9 (protocols 41-45) ------------
 * 1.1.0.0-1.1.0.8: relocated PE (module rows, RVAs). 1.1.0.9: blob at 0x01D00000 like 1.1.1.0 (absolute VAs).
 * site                       signature (16/12 bytes)                         builds
 * CL_CheckFile A, prologue 10 8b 44 24 08 81 ec 04 01 00 00 8d 4c 24 00 50 51  hw 1.1.0.0-1.1.0.8, sw 1.1.0.0-1.1.0.7
 * CL_CheckFile B, prologue 9  55 8b ec 81 ec 04 01 00 00 8b 45 0c 8d 8d fc fe  sw 1.1.0.8
 *   (function that pushes "Download refused, cl_allow_download is 0\n"; 1.1.0.9 = the 1.1.1.0 bytes)
 * FS_FileSize F-hw           51 8b 4c 24 08 8d 44 24 00 56 50 6a               hw all, sw 1.1.0.0-1.1.0.7
 * FS_FileSize F-sw           55 8b ec 51 8b 4d 08 8d 45 fc 56 50               sw 1.1.0.8, 1.1.0.9
 *   (the call after the in-game check in CL_CheckFile, compared with -1)
 * Con_Printf                 per build (rel32 of __chkstk inside); first call in CopyFileFragments
 * Netchan_CopyFileFragments  C0 81 ec 10 01 00 00 53 8b 9c 24 18 01 00 00 55 33  1.1.0.0 (2 args, one stream, L0)
 *   (function with "File   C1 81 ec 10 01 00 00 53 8b 9c 24 18 01 00 00 55 56  1.1.0.1-1.1.0.7
 *   fragment received      C8h 81 ec 14 01 00 00 53 8b 9c 24 1c 01 00 00 55 56 hw 1.1.0.8
 *   with no filename")     C8s 55 8b ec 81 ec 14 01 00 00 53 56 57 8b 7d 08 8b sw 1.1.0.8
 * netchan layouts: L0 1.1.0.0 (ready 0x30c4, bufs 0x2fbc, fragbuf data 0x08 / size 0x10, is-file flag 0x590),
 *   L1 1.1.0.1/1.1.0.4 (0x1ffc, 0x1ff4, 0x0c / 0x14), L2 1.1.0.6+ (0x1fe0, 0x1fd8, 0x10 / 0x18)
 * data, no signature: cl.serverinfo = destination of the "fullserverinfo" handler copy; com_gamedir = first %s
 * of the COM_WriteFile path; cl_allowdownload = fld operand in CL_CheckFile - 12 (name pointer checked).
 * 1.1.0.0-1.1.0.8 copy names unbounded (strcpy into 260 bytes): name_max 259 + ENG_UNBOUNDED_NAMES.
 * cmd_text (1.1.0.4-1.1.0.9, for servers 3.1.0.4-3.1.0.8 that send the resource list together with the
 * "fullserverinfo" command): Cbuf_AddText = the function with "Cbuf_AddText: overflow\n"; site = its
 * 83 c4 04 03 c8 a1 between mov ecx,[&cmd_text.cursize] and mov eax,[&cmd_text.maxsize], both disp32 checked
 * at run time; the value = &cmd_text.data (= maxsize - 4; sizebuf_t data, maxsize, cursize in a row).
 * 1.1.0.0 / 1.1.0.1 are not covered. */
